<article class="env-definition" id="04BK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04BK">Definition <span data-tag="04BK">18.33.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\varphi : \mathcal{O}_1 \to \mathcal{O}_2$ be a homomorphism of sheaves of rings. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an $\mathcal{O}_2$-module. A <em>$\mathcal{O}_1$-derivation</em> or more precisely a <em>$\varphi $-derivation</em> into $\mathcal{F}$ is a map $D : \mathcal{O}_2 \to \mathcal{F}$ which is additive, annihilates the image of $\mathcal{O}_1 \to \mathcal{O}_2$, and satisfies the <em>Leibniz rule</em> </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  D(ab) = aD(b) + D(a)b  \]
</div>
  <p> for all $a, b$ local sections of $\mathcal{O}_2$ (wherever they are both defined). We denote $\text{Der}_{\mathcal{O}_1}(\mathcal{O}_2, \mathcal{F})$ the set of $\varphi $-derivations into $\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article>